From 2ea57e85ac1a20c79605099a48ec8842a3aa0e95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Massee <michael@massee.de>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:19:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tdf#NNNNNN sc UNO: add read-only DisplayedCellBackColor to
 SheetCell

CellBackColor is read from the cell's pattern (direct formatting plus
cell style) via ScCellRangesBase::GetCurrentAttrsDeep(). Conditional
formatting is never evaluated in the UNO layer, so there is no API to
find out which background colour a cell is actually displayed with when
a condition or a colour scale applies. Extensions that render sheet
content themselves (e.g. their own HTML export) therefore lose all
conditionally formatted backgrounds, while the native HTML filter keeps
them because it calls ScDocument::GetCondResult() directly.

Changing CellBackColor itself is not an option: it is a read/write
property describing the set formatting, and code copying properties
between cells would bake the conditional colour into direct formatting.

Add a new read-only SheetCell property DisplayedCellBackColor that uses
the same precedence as ScDocument::FillInfo() for painting: colour scale
colour first, then the background of the cell style applied by a
matching condition, then the cell's own background.

Change-Id: I13529f75132440be612be225801fba01eadc06d4
---
